# Marketing page thumb rule

Every feature, use-case, product, guide, blog, compare, tools, about, and similar marketing page must share the same structure and motion language.

## Page skeleton (in order)

1. `MarketingShell` + JSON-LD
2. `PageHero` — eyebrow, **title ≤ 2 lines**, **intro 2–3 lines**, optional CTAs, optional illustration
3. Optional `VisualBand` (one image moment max near the top)
4. Repeating content blocks via `SectionHeader` + `MotionSection` / `MotionGrid` / `MotionTile`
5. `FaqList` when FAQs exist
6. Related links (compact)
7. `CtaBand`

## Copy limits

- **H1 / section H2**: max **2 lines** visually. Prefer ≤ ~10–12 words. Never a paragraph as a title.
- **Hero intro / section description**: **2–3 lines** max. One job: clarify who it’s for or what you get.
- **Card body**: 1–2 short sentences.
- Avoid India-only framing unless the page is explicitly India-specific SEO.
- Prefer scannable bullets over long prose walls.

## Visual / motion

- Use shared components: `PageHero`, `SectionHeader`, `VisualBand`, `MotionSection`, `MotionGrid`, `MotionTile`, `MediaFrame`, `CtaBand`, `FaqList`.
- Animate with framer-motion via `Reveal` / stagger — expo-out easing (`[0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]`).
- Respect `useReducedMotion`.
- Illustrations only (flat editorial), never photo mockups of code/dashboards in heroes unless intentional product UI.
- Landing homepage may stay text-led; other marketing pages may use illustrations.

## SectionHeader usage

```tsx
<SectionHeader
  eyebrow="Optional"
  title="Short two-line max title"
  description="Two to three lines that explain the section."
/>
```

Do not invent one-off section title styles. Reuse `SectionHeader` + `tile-lift` for cards.
